#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Vortex Entry High-Resolution Diagnostic — with inertial particle ensemble
and **adjoint MPC control** (replaces greedy phase sweep).

Same physics, field construction, rendering, and A/B dynamics as
vortex_entry_hires_inertial.py.  The control method is changed from
greedy per-step phase sweep to a three-phase approach:

  Phase I  — Open-loop phase-sweep carry (identical to greedy version)
             until the vortex is within MPC activation radius of B.
  Phase II — Adjoint MPC: receding-horizon L-BFGS-B optimisation with
             5 DOFs per step (ψ, x_v, y_v, α, β) and discrete adjoint
             gradients.
  Phase III— Settling: α→0 ramp-down, then pure standing-wave recapture.

Outputs:
    results/dev/vortex_entry_hires_inertial_mpc/<timestamp>/
        vortex_entry_hires_mpc_<label>.gif  — animated Gorkov potential
        timeseries.csv                      — per-step metrics
        proximity_vs_time.png               — proximity graph
        convergence.png                     — MPC inner-loop convergence
        particles.csv                       — inertial ensemble (if enabled)
        manifest.json                       — config + metrics

Usage:
    python scripts/dev/vortex_entry_hires_inertial_mpc.py
    python scripts/dev/vortex_entry_hires_inertial_mpc.py --K 15 --T_mpc 2000
    python scripts/dev/vortex_entry_hires_inertial_mpc.py --particle_grid_n 10
"""
